1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:07,136
By the end of this video, you will have sent and received your first shielded payment, with a private note.

2
00:00:08,336 --> 00:00:12,341
Every payment has two sides. Let's start with receiving.

3
00:00:12,691 --> 00:00:18,997
To get paid, tap Receive. Copy your Zcash Shielded Address. It starts with u1.

4
00:00:19,347 --> 00:00:24,649
Send it to the person paying you. They can also scan it if you tap QR Code.

5
00:00:26,149 --> 00:00:32,017
Now sending. Tap Send. Paste the address into Send to, then type the amount.

6
00:00:32,367 --> 00:00:42,097
In Message, you can add a note. A note is a private message that travels with the payment. Only you and the person you pay can read it.

7
00:00:42,447 --> 00:00:43,808
Then tap Review.

8
00:00:45,307 --> 00:00:51,934
Before anything is sent, Zodl shows the Confirmation screen. Check the address and the fee.

9
00:00:52,284 --> 00:01:01,943
Zcash fees follow a public rule called ZIP 317. The smallest fee is 0.0001 ZEC.

10
00:01:02,293 --> 00:01:07,931
Tap Send. When Zodl shows Sent!, your first shielded payment is on its way.

11
00:01:09,731 --> 00:01:15,643
On your friend's phone, the payment arrives with your note. Only the two of you can read it.

12
00:01:15,993 --> 00:01:22,691
Ask them to send a little back to your u1 address. Now you have received a shielded payment too.

13
00:01:24,192 --> 00:01:32,499
And what does the blockchain show? Only scrambled data. Not who paid. Not who got paid. Not how much. Not the note.

14
00:01:33,998 --> 00:01:35,829
You did it. You're shielded.

15
00:01:39,498 --> 00:01:43,530
Tick Sending and Receiving on the site to finish your checklist.

16
00:01:46,498 --> 00:01:54,464
Episode 5 shows five habits that keep it private. Find it at zero-to-shielded.vercel.app.
